### IMPORTANT: How to use this file
### 1. First run Section 2 (login requests) to get tokens
### 2. Copy the access_token and refresh_token from login responses
### 3. Paste them into the constants above (adminToken, physicianToken, etc.)
### 4. Then run other sections using these pre-defined tokens
### 5. When you create resources, copy their IDs to the constants above
### 6. This allows testing without automatic response parsing

### ============================================================================
### API SECTIONS OVERVIEW
### ============================================================================
### SECTION 1:  Health & Connectivity Checks
### SECTION 2:  Authentication Module (register, login, refresh)
### SECTION 3:  Users Module (admin & physician management)
### SECTION 4:  Patients Module (create, read, update, delete)
###             ⭐ NOW REQUIRES X-RAY IMAGE DATA (imageBase64 field)
###             ⭐ Automatically creates X-ray record on patient creation
### SECTION 5:  X-Ray Module (X-ray image management)
### SECTION 6:  ML Model Validation (X-ray validation)
### SECTION 7:  ML TB Prediction (TB detection prediction)
### SECTION 8:  System Logging (audit trail of all operations) [NEW]
### SECTION 9:  Authentication Logging (login/logout tracking) [NEW]
### SECTION 10: Diagnosis Results (TB diagnosis records)
### SECTION 11: ML Model Sync Verification (direct ML service testing)
### SECTION 12: Complete Workflow Test (end-to-end scenario)
### SECTION 13: Error Scenarios & Edge Cases
### SECTION 14: Performance & Load Testing Notes
### SECTION 15: Testing Guidelines & Configuration
###
### 🆕 NEW FEATURES IN THIS VERSION:
### - Comprehensive audit logging (SystemLoggingService)
### - Authentication event tracking (AuthLoggingService)
### - Required X-ray image data for patient registration
### - Automatic diagnosis generation from ML pipeline

