### SECTION 4: PATIENTS MODULE
### ============================================================================

### 4.1 Create Patient WITH X-RAY DATA (REQUIRED) - JSON Method with Base64
### ✅ IMPORTANT VALIDATIONS PERFORMED:
### 1. ✔️ ML service health check (must be running)
### 2. ✔️ X-ray image format validation (JPEG/PNG/DICOM)
### 3. ✔️ X-ray validity check via AI model (confidence > 0.7)
### 4. ✔️ TB diagnosis prediction (automatic)
###
### RETURNS 400 BAD REQUEST IF:
### - ML service is not running/healthy
### - X-ray image is not a valid image format
### - X-ray fails validation (not a valid medical X-ray)
### - No X-ray image provided
###
### METHOD 1: Provide X-ray as base64 string in JSON payload
# @name createPatient
POST {{baseUrl}}/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "phone": "+1234567890",
  "dateOfBirth": "1980-05-15",
  "gender": "Male",
  "medicalHistory": "Hypertension, Diabetes",
  "allergies": "Penicillin",
  "medications": "Metformin 500mg twice daily",
  "address": "123 Main Street",
  "city": "New York",
  "state": "NY",
  "postalCode": "10001",
  "country": "USA",
  "imageBase64": "",
  "fileName": "chest_xray_pa.jpg",
  "xrayType": "Chest PA",
  "xrayNotes": "Routine TB screening X-ray"
}


###get  patients

### 📌 Response Includes:
### - Patient details
### - X-ray validation status (valid/invalid)
### - TB diagnosis prediction result (if X-ray valid)
### - Diagnosis confidence level
### - Recommendations based on TB intensity

### 4.1B Create Patient - FILE UPLOAD METHOD (Multipart Form Data)
### ✅ METHOD 2: Upload X-ray image file directly (auto-convert to base64)
### Supported formats: JPEG, PNG, DICOM (up to 50MB)
# @name createPatientWithFile
POST {{baseUrl}}/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

