### SECTION 5: X-RAY MODULE
### ============================================================================
### ⭐ NOTE: X-rays are automatically created when registering patients (Section 4.1)
### The endpoint below is for manual X-ray creation/updates when needed

### 5.1 Create X-Ray (Manual - Usually automatic via patient registration)
# @name createXray
POST {{baseUrl}}/xrays
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "fileName": "chest_xray_front.jpg",
  "imageBase64": "",
  "xrayType": "Chest PA",
  "notes": "Routine chest X-ray for TB screening"
}

### Extract X-Ray ID
### Copy id from response above and paste into @xrayId at the top

### 5.2 Get All X-Rays
GET {{baseUrl}}/xrays
Authorization: Bearer {{{{adminToken}}}}
Accept: application/json

### 5.3 Get X-Ray by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/xrays/{{xrayId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 5.4 List X-Rays (filter patientId on client-side from GET /xrays)
GET {{baseUrl}}/xrays?patientId={{patientId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 5.5 Update X-Ray Status
PUT {{baseUrl}}/xrays/{{xrayId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "processed",
  "qualityScore": 0.95
}

### 5.6 Delete X-Ray
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/xrays/{{xrayId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}

---

### SECTION 6: ML MODEL VALIDATION (X-RAY VALIDATION)
### ============================================================================

### 6.1 Validate X-Ray via API
POST {{baseUrl}}/validation/xray
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imageBase64": "",
  "fileName": "chest_xray.jpg"
}

### Check validation response
### Expected: { is_xray: true, confidence: 0.95-0.99, prediction: "Valid X-Ray" }

---

### SECTION 7: TB PREDICTION MODULE (ML MODEL INTEGRATION)
### ============================================================================

### 7.1 Predict TB from Base64 Image
# @name predictTB
POST {{baseUrl}}/predict/tb/base64
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imageBase64": "",
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}"
}

### Expected Response:
### { 
###   "tb_detected": true/false,
###   "confidence": 0.0-1.0,
###   "prediction": "TB detected" or "No TB detected",
###   "heatmap_base64": "...",
###   "mlModel": "tb_classifier.pth"
### }

---

