### SECTION 12: COMPLETE WORKFLOW TEST (End-to-End)
### ============================================================================

### 12.1 Complete TB Detection Workflow:
### 1. Register user
### 2. Login user
### 3. Create patient
### 4. Create X-Ray record
### 5. Validate X-Ray (ML Service)
### 6. Run TB Prediction (ML Service)
### 7. Create Diagnosis Result
### 8. Retrieve all results

### Steps:
### - Run Section 2 (Login Physician)
### - Run Section 4.1 (Create Patient with X-ray)
### - Run Section 6.1 (Validate X-Ray - usually automatic)
### - Run Section 7.1 (Predict TB - usually automatic)
### - Run Section 10.1 (Create Diagnosis - usually automatic)
### - Run Section 10.2 (Get All Diagnosis Results)

---

### SECTION 13: ERROR SCENARIOS & EDGE CASES
### ============================================================================

### 13.1 Test Unauthorized Access
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

### 13.2 Test Missing Required Fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - Schema validation error

### 13.3 Test Invalid Patient ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/patients/invalid-uuid-format
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request or 404 Not Found

### 13.4 Test Non-existent Resource
GET {{baseUrl}}/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{physicianToken}}

### Expected: 404 Not Found

---

### SECTION 14: PERFORMANCE & LOAD TESTING NOTES
### ============================================================================

### Notes for Performance Testing:
### - TB Prediction typically takes 2-5 seconds (GPU-dependent)
### - X-Ray Validation typically takes 1-2 seconds
### - Database queries should complete in <100ms
### - API response times should be <5 seconds
### 
### To run load tests, use Apache JMeter or k6:
### k6 run performance-test.js
###
### Monitor:
### - Database connection pool (max 20 connections)
### - ML Service throughput (handle queue if needed)
### - Memory usage (watch for memory leaks)
### - CPU usage during predictions

---

### SECTION 15: TESTING GUIDELINES & CONFIGURATION
### ============================================================================
### 1. Update @baseUrl if API is not on localhost:3000
### 2. Update @mlServiceUrl if ML service is not on localhost:5000
### 3. Replace {{userId}}, {{patientId}}, {{xrayId}} with actual IDs from responses
### 4. The @adminToken and @physicianToken are extracted from login responses
### 5. All timestamps are auto-generated by the backend
### 6. For file uploads, use form-data instead of base64 for larger images
### 7. Check headers: Content-Type, Authorization are required for protected routes
### 8. Database schema is auto-synced on startup (TYPEORM_SYNCHRONIZE=true)
### 9. All enums are type-safe and validated
### 10. ML models must be in /cnn_models/pth_files/ directory
